            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Wars and Conflicts</strong><br>\nIn the following decades, Israel was involved in a series of wars and conflicts, including the Six-Day War of 1967 and the Yom Kippur War of 1973. These wars led to significant territorial changes and had a lasting impact on the geopolitical landscape of the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Peace Agreements</strong><br>\nIn the 1990s, Israel took steps to make peace with some of its Arab neighbors. The Oslo Accords of 1993 and the peace treaty with Jordan in 1994 were significant milestones on the path to a more peaceful region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Current Challenges and Future Perspectives</strong><br>\nToday, Israel faces many challenges, both internally and externally. The question of a two-state solution with the Palestinians, the threat from Iran, and internal political tensions are just a few of the issues shaping the country in the present and future.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
